# 🚀 Arrays and Slices in Go

## 📖 What is an Array?

An **Array** is a collection of elements of the same data type stored in contiguous memory locations.

* Fixed Size
* Same Data Type
* Indexed from 0

---

# 🔹 Array Declaration

## Syntax

```go
var arrayName [size]dataType
```

### Example

```go
package main

import "fmt"

func main() {
    var numbers [5]int

    numbers[0] = 10
    numbers[1] = 20
    numbers[2] = 30
    numbers[3] = 40
    numbers[4] = 50

    fmt.Println(numbers)
}
```

### Output

```text
[10 20 30 40 50]
```

---

# 🔹 Initialize an Array

```go
package main

import "fmt"

func main() {
    marks := [5]int{80, 75, 90, 85, 95}

    fmt.Println(marks)
}
```

### Output

```text
[80 75 90 85 95]
```

---

# 🔹 Access Array Elements

```go
package main

import "fmt"

func main() {
    fruits := [3]string{"Apple", "Banana", "Mango"}

    fmt.Println(fruits[0])
    fmt.Println(fruits[1])
}
```

### Output

```text
Apple
Banana
```

---

# 🔹 Loop Through an Array

```go
package main

import "fmt"

func main() {
    numbers := [5]int{10, 20, 30, 40, 50}

    for i := 0; i < len(numbers); i++ {
        fmt.Println(numbers[i])
    }
}
```

