# 📝 Real-Life Array Problems

## Problem 1: Store Student Marks

```go
package main

import "fmt"

func main() {
    marks := [5]int{85, 90, 75, 80, 95}

    fmt.Println(marks)
}
```

---

## Problem 2: Find Sum of Array Elements

```go
package main

import "fmt"

func main() {
    numbers := [5]int{10, 20, 30, 40, 50}

    sum := 0

    for i := 0; i < len(numbers); i++ {
        sum += numbers[i]
    }

    fmt.Println("Sum =", sum)
}
```

### Output

```text
Sum = 150
```

---

## Problem 3: Find Largest Number

```go
package main

import "fmt"

func main() {
    numbers := [5]int{25, 18, 45, 10, 35}

    largest := numbers[0]

    for i := 1; i < len(numbers); i++ {
        if numbers[i] > largest {
            largest = numbers[i]
        }
    }

    fmt.Println("Largest =", largest)
}
```

